  "result": "`click.KeyValue` is added and `python -m pytest tests/test_types.py -q` passes (45 passed, 2 skipped).\n\n- **Type:** `KeyValue` is a `ParamType` subclass in `src/click/types.py`, placed right after `UUIDParameterType`. Its `name` is `\"key=value\"`.\n- **Parsing:** `convert()` splits on the first `=` only, so `a=b=c` gives `('a', 'b=c')` and `a=` gives `('a', '')`.\n- **Errors:** input with no `=` or an empty key fails via `self.fail(...)` with `'...' is not a valid key=value pair.`\n- **Export:** the class itself is exported from `src/click/__init__.py`.\n- **Tests:** two new tests in `tests/test_types.py` cover valid splitting (including `=` in the value and an empty value) and the failure cases `novalue`, `=value` and an empty string.\n\nI did not run the full suite, only `tests/test_types.py`.",
